title: Log endpoints
tags: [[Event log]]
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: GET /log (bounded two ways), the change feed GET /log/since, one revision in detail, and setting a label.

|!Route |!Does |
|<<cmd "GET /repos/:repo/log">> |the history, as operations and revisions (below) |
|<<cmd "GET /repos/:repo/log/since">> `?op=<id>` |the change feed: the newest operation, and every operation created after `op` |
|<<cmd "GET /repos/:repo/log/revisions/:rev_id">> |one revision with all its operations and their snapshots; `head` for the newest |
|<<cmd "PATCH /repos/:repo/log/revisions/:rev_id">> |`{"label": "…"}` or `{"label": null}` |

!! GET /log

|!Parameter |!Default |!Does |
|`metarecord_uuid` |— |only the operations of that metarecord |
|`limit` |— |at most this many operations, the newest |
|`revisions` |— |at most this many revisions, the newest — whole unless `limit` cuts the oldest |
|`since`, `until` |— |only operations in revisions timestamped within (Unix ms) |
|`include_snapshots` |`false` |each operation with `snapshots_before`/`snapshots_after` |

```
{"head": 3, "first": 1,
 "operations": [{"id": 1, "rev_id": 1, "seq": 1, "op_type": "create_metarecord",
                 "entity_uuid": "…", "field_name": null, "reverts_op_id": null}, …],
 "revisions": [{"id": 1, "timestamp": 1700000000000, "label": null, "origin": null}, …],
 "total_operations": 3, "total_revisions": 2}
```

Operations run oldest first — the log is a sequence ([[The operation log]]). `head` is the
newest operation, `first` the oldest still in the log — where undo stops ([[The undo selection]]). `revisions` lists only those the returned operations belong to; a revision
cut by `limit` carries `"partial": true` and `op_count`. The totals describe the ''whole''
log, whatever the window. Bounds limit the read itself, and a filter widens it until it
finds what was asked ([[Reading the log costs the window]]).

!! GET /log/since

The change feed clients poll: the current `head` and every operation created after `op`,
each naming its `entity_uuid`. Without `op`, just the head. The log only grows, so `head`
only moves forward. A delta larger than `limit` (default 500) comes back `truncated` and
empty, and a client falls back to a full refresh. The GUI's change feed is built on it.

!! One revision

`GET /log/revisions/:rev_id` always includes snapshots (it is for the detail view):
`{"revision": {"id", "timestamp", "label", "origin", "is_head", "operation_count"},
"operations": [{"id", "seq", "op_type", "entity_uuid", "field_name", "snapshots_before",
"snapshots_after"}, …]}`, a snapshot being a row in column form
(`{"field_id": 43, "field_name": "rating", "value_type": "int", "value_int": 3}`). A
revision may hold a whole reconcile, so `offset`/`limit` window its operations and `op`
picks one (`404` if not in it); `is_head` and `operation_count` always describe the whole
revision. `404` for an unknown revision.
